@vector.tf bugbot said this, Missing cross-module dependency validation for vector

Medium Severity

The vector module depends on external_secrets at runtime (it passes external_secrets_cluster_store_name referencing a ClusterSecretStore), but there is no plan-time validation to ensure external_secrets is also enabled. The auto-generated README even documents an external_external.vector_validate data source (line 81, newly added) that doesn't exist in the code — following the established application_deployment_validate pattern. If vector is enabled but external_secrets is disabled via overrides, the deployment will fail at Kubernetes runtime instead of being caught at terraform plan

